config RING_IPHONE_LOGIC
	bool "Ring iPhone logic: ANCS response reassembly, AMS decoder (pure)"
	select RING_INBOX
	select RING_TIME_LOGIC
	help
	  No kernel, driver or Bluetooth call.

config RING_IPHONE
	bool "Ring iPhone: notifications and actions, media, time from an iPhone"
	select RING_IPHONE_LOGIC
	select RING_TIME
	select RING_DEVICES
	select BT_GATT_CLIENT
	select BT_GATT_DM
	select BT_GATTP
	select BT_ANCS_CLIENT
	select BT_AMS_CLIENT
	select BT_CTS_CLIENT
	depends on BT_PERIPHERAL && BT_SMP
	help
	  After the link of the active device reaches security level 4 the ring looks for Apple's
	  three services (Notification Center, Media, Current Time) and for Service Changed. A device
	  without them (Android, Mac) is not an error. Nothing received here can start or stop a recording.

config RING_IPHONE_FETCH_QUEUE
	int "Notifications waiting for their attributes"
	default 32
	range 1 255
	depends on RING_IPHONE
	help
	  The iPhone sends every notification it holds when the ring subscribes. The ring asks for the
	  attributes of one at a time. An id that does not fit is not fetched (counted).
